  "note": "Shadowsocks-2022 per-user PSK (uPSK) derived from the user uuid. Derived TWICE in this repository, in two languages: the panel derives it for the subscription URI (apps/panel-backend/src/lib/credentials.ts, deriveSsPassword) and the node derives it for the SS config it writes (apps/node/internal/core/sscreds.go, DeriveSsPassword). If the two ever disagree, the key in the client URI stops matching the key on the node and every shadowsocks user fails authentication, silently. These vectors are the contract: both sides have a test that reads this file, so a change on either side reddens on that side. Regenerating them is a deliberate act - it rotates the key of every existing shadowsocks user.",
  "algorithm": "base64_standard(sha256(`${uuid}:ss`)[0..keyLen]), keyLen = 16 for 2022-blake3-aes-128-gcm, else 32",
